{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Cruelty</b> — this word is joined to wisdom, for it issues from it." "<b>And the overflow</b> — a hint to the act of one who acts in his anger, that it is like overflowing waters. That is: cruelty from heat [חמה] and overflow from anger [אף] are akin to being severe, and who can stand before a jealous man, for it is harder and fiercer than both, for it gives birth to them. And the proof: 'the jealousy of a man is heat [חמת גבר]' — and the meaning is that jealousy gives birth to his heat."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:00.468481468Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}